# Every environment variable this stack reads, with blank or placeholder values.
# NEVER put a real value in this file - it is tracked, and the repository is public.
# `*.env` and `secrets/` are git-ignored; this `.example` file is the one exception.

# --- On the box: ~/ai-stack/secrets/api-key.env ------------------------------
# Bearer tokens for llama-swap - ONE PER CONSUMER. Loaded by
# systemd/llama-swap.service (EnvironmentFile) and substituted into
# llama-swap.yaml through env macros; bin/run-openwebui.sh sources it too.
#
# Install:
#   umask 077
#   cp secrets.env.example ~/ai-stack/secrets/api-key.env
#   chmod 600 ~/ai-stack/secrets/api-key.env       # owner read/write, nobody else
#   chmod 700 ~/ai-stack/secrets
# then fill in every key below.
#
# Generate one key (run once PER VARIABLE - never reuse a value):
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# 64 hex characters = 256 bits. Hex is deliberate: no spaces (llama-swap
# rejects keys containing spaces), no quotes, nothing a shell, systemd's
# EnvironmentFile parser or YAML will reinterpret. To add keys without ever
# displaying them:
#   umask 077; for v in LLM_KEY_...; do grep -q "^$v=" api-key.env || \
#     printf '%s=%s\n' "$v" "$(openssl rand -hex 32)" >> api-key.env; done
#
# Rules llama-swap enforces - break one and the service will NOT START, which
# takes the endpoint down for every consumer:
#   - every variable referenced in llama-swap.yaml must be set AND non-empty
#   - a value must not contain spaces
# Preflight before any restart:  llama-swap -config llama-swap.yaml -validate
# (run with this file loaded into the environment).
# Format rules for this file (it is read by systemd AND sourced by bash):
#   - NAME=value, no spaces around "=", no quotes, no "export", one per line
#
# Naming: consumer "agent-host1" -> LLM_KEY_AGENT_HOST1 (upper-case, "-" -> "_").
# Add a variable here AND a matching line under apiKeys in llama-swap.yaml for
# every additional host. Do not share one key between two hosts.
#
# Never paste a value into a commit, an issue, a chat, or a shell command line
# (command lines land in shell history and in the process list).

# legacy: the original shared key. Kept valid during migration so no consumer
# breaks at cutover; remove the variable and its apiKeys line at a later
# planned reload, once every consumer has its own key.
LLM_API_KEY=

# agent-<host>: coding agents on one operator workstation
LLM_KEY_AGENT_HOST1=

# dashboard-<host>: one always-on dashboard / kiosk client per host
LLM_KEY_DASHBOARD_HOST1=
LLM_KEY_DASHBOARD_HOST2=

# cluster-assistant: an assistant service running in a cluster
LLM_KEY_CLUSTER_ASSISTANT=

# sandbox-agent: agent sandboxes running on this box
LLM_KEY_SANDBOX_AGENT=

# webui: the Open WebUI container on this box (read by bin/run-openwebui.sh)
LLM_KEY_WEBUI=

# standby: pre-issued spare held by NO consumer. Used by the rotation runbook
# (README -> Operations -> Keys and rotation) so a consumer can be moved to a
# key that is already accepted, without restarting anything.
LLM_KEY_STANDBY=

# Optional. Served context length for bin/run-qwen38.sh; blank = 500000.
# (examples/run-gpt-oss.sh reads it too; blank = 131072.)
CTX_LEN=

# HOME is also read - llama-swap.yaml uses an env macro for it and the launchers
# use $HOME. systemd sets it for a user service; do not set it here.

# --- One-time host setup: bin/privileged-setup.sh, bin/enable-firewall.sh ----
# Local subnet in CIDR form, allowed through ufw. Can be passed as the first
# argument instead. No default: a private-network address never goes in the repo.
LAN_CIDR=
# Account that owns the stack (linger). Blank = the account that ran sudo.
STACK_USER=

# --- Benchmark clients only: scripts/depth-concurrency.sh, scripts/mixed-workload.sh
# Endpoint, e.g. http://<spark-ip>:9292. No default, for the same reason.
LLM_HOST=
# A bearer token accepted by the endpoint, under the name the clients expect.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Issue number where the load-test window was announced. The box is shared; the
# script refuses to run without it. See AGENTS.md.
ANNOUNCED_ISSUE=
# Set to 1 to print the plan and contact nothing.
DRY_RUN=
